1. Start the FastAPI receiver:
python -m uvicorn utils.webhook_test_server:app --port 8000

2. In a separate terminal, start the ngrok tunnel bound to your reserved domain:
ngrok http --url=nestlike-unpoignantly-orville.ngrok-free.dev 8000

Notes:
- Run them in that order — ngrok needs port 8000 already listening.
- Keep both terminals open; closing either kills that piece (server or tunnel).
- Captured payloads land in captured_payloads.jsonl at the project root — each line is one JSON event.
- Health check once both are up: curl https://nestlike-unpoignantly-orville.ngrok-free.dev/health should return {"status":"ok"}.
- The domain is reserved to your ngrok account, so it stays the same every time — no need to update the Unipile webhook URL.